WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:42.251 --> 00:00:43.460 size:43% position:48%,middle line:85%
My name is Aisha.

00:05:11.853 --> 00:05:15.440 size:53% position:47%,middle line:79%
I was raised in Gifu,
in the countryside.

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:18.860 size:75% line:79%
- Chipa: The countryside.
- Yes, so besides my siblings,

00:05:18.860 --> 00:05:23.406 size:70% line:79%
I had never seen anyone
who had the same skin color.

00:05:23.406 --> 00:05:28.161 size:53% position:47%,middle line:85%
I was always bullied,

00:05:28.161 --> 00:05:33.416 size:78% position:44%,middle line:79%
so I always asked my mom
why she married a Black person.

00:05:33.416 --> 00:05:39.005 size:53% position:47%,middle line:10%
Why was I born
with this skin color?

00:05:39.005 --> 00:05:44.469 size:61% line:79%
But now I respect myself
and love my skin color.

00:05:44.469 --> 00:05:49.683 size:56% line:79%
Just three months ago,
I traveled to Nigeria

00:05:49.683 --> 00:05:55.188 size:61% line:79%
and I saw so many people
bleaching their skin.

00:05:55.188 --> 00:05:56.773 size:56% line:85%
It made me really sad.

00:07:23.318 --> 00:07:24.903 size:48% position:48%,middle line:79%
I really like those
English lyrics.

00:07:24.903 --> 00:07:26.446 size:50% line:85%
Thank you very much.

00:07:26.446 --> 00:07:29.324 size:53% position:47%,middle line:79%
She comes from
a diverse background.

00:07:29.324 --> 00:07:33.453 size:53% position:47%,middle line:79%
<i> She has the Japanese
 "cool" side...</i>

00:07:37.248 --> 00:07:42.087 size:75% line:79%
...and then the American Black
"groove" and open mind.

00:07:58.978 --> 00:08:01.815 size:38% position:48%,middle line:85%
<i> I am Japanese,</i>

00:08:01.815 --> 00:08:03.358 size:58% position:47%,middle line:85%
but I have Black roots,

00:08:03.358 --> 00:08:05.652 size:65% line:79%
and on the outside
I look like a Black woman,

00:08:05.652 --> 00:08:09.572 size:58% position:47%,middle line:79%
<i> but I am still
 a Japanese woman, too.</i>

00:08:09.572 --> 00:08:12.242 size:56% line:85%
I was born in Nigeria.

00:08:12.242 --> 00:08:17.122 size:68% position:46%,middle line:79%
<i> My parents divorced
 when I was five years old.</i>

00:08:17.122 --> 00:08:20.375 size:73% position:45%,middle line:79%
<i> After that, I lived together
 with my sibling and my mom</i>

00:08:20.375 --> 00:08:24.003 size:43% position:48%,middle line:79%
<i> and grandparents
 at their house.</i>

00:08:24.003 --> 00:08:27.257 size:48% position:48%,middle line:85%
Since I look Black,

00:08:27.257 --> 00:08:30.927 size:75% line:79%
<i> a lot of people would call me
 "foreigner, foreigner."</i>

00:08:30.927 --> 00:08:34.973 size:61% line:79%
In school, I tried to be
even more Japanese

00:08:34.973 --> 00:08:38.977 size:68% position:46%,middle line:85%
<i> than the girls my own age.</i>

00:08:40.562 --> 00:08:43.440 size:61% line:79%
<i> Being in an environment
 where I felt like</i>

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:45.734 size:61% line:79%
I had to change who I am
in order to be accepted

00:08:45.734 --> 00:08:49.237 size:58% position:47%,middle line:74%
<i> was very stressful
 to go through
 when you were a child.</i>

00:08:49.237 --> 00:08:52.282 size:56% line:79%
I would like to change
this situation

00:08:52.282 --> 00:08:58.371 size:45% line:79%
for even one child
in the future.

00:10:31.214 --> 00:10:33.883 size:61% line:10%
As for me, I am biracial
Japanese and Nigerian.

00:10:33.883 --> 00:10:35.844 size:56% line:10%
I was raised in Japan,

00:10:35.844 --> 00:10:38.179 size:53% position:47%,middle line:79%
and my first language
is Japanese.

00:10:38.179 --> 00:10:42.600 size:50% line:74%
So when I date
a Japanese person,
we have no problems.

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:44.060 size:53% position:47%,middle line:79%
Chipa: You understand
the conversation.

00:10:44.060 --> 00:10:46.479 size:48% position:48%,middle line:85%
Yes, yes, yes, yes.

00:10:46.479 --> 00:10:48.523 size:75% line:79%
One thing we are talking about
is a difference in culture,

00:10:48.523 --> 00:10:50.191 size:75% line:79%
but what you're saying is that
you don't have a difference

00:10:50.191 --> 00:10:53.111 size:63% position:47%,middle line:79%
in culture
(in dating Japanese men).

00:10:53.111 --> 00:10:57.323 size:63% position:47%,middle line:74%
So which is the problem?
Is it the Japanese person
or us foreigners?

00:10:57.323 --> 00:11:00.118 size:68% position:46%,middle line:79%
Chipa: For me, when I think
about why it's difficult

00:11:00.118 --> 00:11:03.162 size:68% position:46%,middle line:79%
to date Japanese people--
when we have conversations,

00:11:03.162 --> 00:11:06.541 size:56% line:79%
the depth isn't there.
It's surface level.

00:11:06.541 --> 00:11:08.501 size:48% position:48%,middle line:85%
It's surface level.

00:12:39.550 --> 00:12:41.177 size:50% line:79%
You don't need to be
embarrassed.

00:14:09.682 --> 00:14:14.312 size:70% line:79%
I was in Miss Universe Japan
in 2020.

00:14:18.566 --> 00:14:21.903 size:78% position:44%,middle line:79%
On the way home from rehearsal,
the police stopped me

00:14:21.903 --> 00:14:26.032 size:73% position:45%,middle line:85%
and it was just before 12 AM.

00:14:26.032 --> 00:14:31.204 size:78% position:44%,middle line:74%
I was holding a big bag
and walking around the station,
so the police stopped me.

00:14:31.204 --> 00:14:34.665 size:75% line:74%
They asked me
what was in my bag and whether
they could search my bag.

00:14:34.665 --> 00:14:36.709 size:53% position:47%,middle line:79%
- Aisha: 12 at night?
- Raimu: 12 at night.

00:14:36.709 --> 00:14:39.921 size:70% line:74%
This was the first time
in my life that
a police officer stopped me.

00:14:39.921 --> 00:14:47.595 size:61% line:74%
At that time,
I thought it was because
I looked Black.

00:14:47.595 --> 00:14:54.685 size:75% line:79%
I felt shocked that they would
do something like that

00:14:54.685 --> 00:14:58.689 size:56% line:85%
based on how I looked.

00:14:58.689 --> 00:15:00.858 size:73% position:45%,middle line:79%
So I had slightly complicated
feelings about this.

00:18:17.138 --> 00:18:19.390 size:70% line:85%
Oh, really? ...Is that so...

00:18:40.369 --> 00:18:41.495 size:23% position:48%,middle line:85%
Be quiet.

00:21:58.400 --> 00:22:00.319 size:73% position:45%,middle line:85%
When I decided I wanted to be

00:22:00.319 --> 00:22:02.404 size:68% position:46%,middle line:79%
part of
the entertainment industry,

00:22:02.404 --> 00:22:04.990 size:75% line:79%
I feel there are still limited
opportunities in Japan,

00:22:04.990 --> 00:22:06.242 size:65% line:85%
and I want to change that.

00:22:06.242 --> 00:22:08.369 size:41% line:85%
For that reason,

00:22:08.369 --> 00:22:13.541 size:78% position:44%,middle line:85%
I feel I need to stay in Japan.

00:22:13.541 --> 00:22:15.834 size:25% line:85%
As for me,

00:22:15.834 --> 00:22:19.630 size:63% position:47%,middle line:79%
I've been living in Japan
since I was a child.

00:24:35.265 --> 00:24:38.060 size:45% line:79%
<i> Through my work,
 my goal and dream</i>

00:24:38.060 --> 00:24:42.064 size:58% position:47%,middle line:79%
was to give inspiration
to children

00:24:42.064 --> 00:24:45.776 size:63% position:47%,middle line:85%
by playing diverse roles.

00:24:45.776 --> 00:24:47.569 size:75% line:85%
<i> Right now, through my acting,</i>

00:24:47.569 --> 00:24:51.156 size:58% position:47%,middle line:79%
<i> I want to give kids
 of the next generation</i>

00:24:51.156 --> 00:24:54.076 size:56% line:85%
hope for their dreams.

00:26:19.203 --> 00:26:20.871 size:38% position:48%,middle line:10%
I think instead

00:26:20.871 --> 00:26:22.456 size:53% position:47%,middle line:10%
of being offended,
we should teach them.

